1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,750
In 1324, a king walked into Cairo, and broke its economy.

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,570
Not with an army. With gifts.

3
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:16,870
His name was Mansa Musa, ruler of the Mali Empire, often called the richest man who ever lived.

4
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:22,830
His kingdom was rich in gold, at a time when the whole world ran on it.

5
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:27,010
That year, he set out for Mecca, across the Sahara.

6
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:34,090
By some accounts, tens of thousands of people travelled with him, and camels loaded with gold.

7
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:38,110
When he reached Cairo, he gave it away. To officials.

8
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,290
To merchants. To the poor in the streets.

9
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,870
And then, something strange happened.

10
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:50,330
There was so much gold in Cairo, that gold itself became cheap.

11
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:52,190
Its value fell.

12
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:57,230
And according to one historian, 12 years later, it still hadn't recovered.

13
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:02,670
One man's generosity shook one of the richest cities on Earth.

14
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:06,730
But it also put Mali on the map. Literally.

15
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:14,070
50 years later, a famous map of the world showed him on a throne, holding a nugget of gold.

16
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,950
Most people are remembered for what they kept.

17
00:01:18,090 --> 00:01:20,510
He was remembered for what he gave away.

